      claude: `Act as a pragmatist architect for a solo builder shipping a weekend prototype that may or may not survive the weekend. Argue SQLite locally and Postgres only if the app graduates: what SQLite already gives (real schema, constraints, transactions, typed migrations through the ORM), what it does not (networked access, many writers, managed backups), and the precise migration checklist for the day it matters. Kill the instinct to provision a cloud database before the first user exists. Under 16 lines.`,
      chatgpt: `My app is a personal tool running on my laptop. I keep seeing tutorials spin up a cloud Postgres before writing any code - but I also read SQLite is a real database. What can SQLite honestly do, when does it stop being enough, and how painful is the move from a file to a server database later?`,
