      generic: `Design direct-to-storage uploads: the server signs a short, limited permission (presigned PUT or client token), the browser sends bytes straight to storage with progress events, chunked multipart above the single-request ceiling, and a server-side finalize that verifies the object before trusting the client - keeping access keys off the browser entirely.`,
