      claude: `Act as an edge-caching consultant. Explain the three header decisions for a static host serving an SPA plus API: fingerprinted assets (cache forever, immutable - because the name changes when bytes do), index.html (never cache, or users of the old page fetch the new JS by a name that no longer exists - the half-deploy bug), and public API GETs (short s-maxage with the staleness budget named aloud, or no-store). Give the curl commands that prove each and the one mistake that ships the wrong pair (copy-pasting the asset policy onto html). Under 18 lines.`,
