      claude: `Act as a media-pipeline engineer. For a marketplace with user photos shown at 6 sizes across mobile and desktop, compare: pre-generating crops at upload (storage × sizes, rigid), on-the-fly CDN transforms (one original, URL parameters, first-hit cost then cache), and client-side CSS cropping (still downloads everything). Give the transform URL shape with width, quality and format, the caching that makes repeated hits free, and the two guardrails (sign or allow-list the parameters publicly, cap the maximum width you will render). Under 18 lines.`,
      chatgpt: `Users upload profile pictures of random sizes and my app shows them in tiny circles, cards and big previews. Right now I download whatever they uploaded at full size every time. Is there a way to have one file that just... resizes itself in the link? Explain image CDNs like Cloudinary plainly, the cost, and the free-tier reality check.`,
